# Obsidian Vault & Plugin Discovery and Installation Protocol

This reference document outlines the deterministic procedure for discovering local Obsidian vaults on macOS, manually installing community plugins from GitHub releases, seeding default plugin configurations, and handling LLM provider authentication (notably Google Cloud & Gemini).

---

## 1. Vault Discovery via System Configuration

On macOS, Obsidian stores vault registry and window states in:
`~/Library/Application Support/obsidian/obsidian.json`

### Python Vault Discovery Recipe:
```python
import json, os

config_path = os.path.expanduser('~/Library/Application Support/obsidian/obsidian.json')
if os.path.exists(config_path):
    with open(config_path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:
        data = json.load(f)
    vaults = data.get('vaults', {})
    for vault_id, info in vaults.items():
        is_open = info.get('open', False)
        path = info.get('path')
        print(f"Vault: {path} (Open: {is_open})")
```

The currently active vault will have `"open": true`.

